\newlabel{fig:scalar-couplings}{{S1}{7}{Supporting scalar classification experiment: all three fixed steps in the predeclared zero-start final-window display. Left: normalized population risks for both optimizers and both rank couplings. Right: opposite/equal-rank risk ratios. Empirical error bars are approximate pointwise 95\% intervals. Shading represents separately computed independent asymptotic oracle enclosures (joint 99\% oracle event), excluding unknown finite-step errors. The two uncertainty statements are not a combined coverage guarantee. Both AdamW arms have higher absolute risk than SGD. Plotting code was developed with OpenAI Codex; displayed quantities are derived from recorded numerical outputs}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{tab:decay-response}{{S1}{7}{Prospective Paired-Decay Response at the Final Window}{table.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:decay-contrast}{{S2}{8}{Companion paired-decay response: the complete predeclared zero-start final-window display at both rates, normalized by $\delta =r^{1-\gamma }$. Red error bars are approximate simultaneous 95\% bands from the full 18-coordinate primary family. Shading is the separately frozen response-functional enclosure (98\% joint oracle event); its unknown finite-rate remainder and equilibration error are excluded. The dashed zero line is the cancelled leading contrast. The plot fits no exponent and does not retrospectively validate the preserved earlier absolute predictions. Plotting code was developed with OpenAI Codex; displayed quantities are derived from recorded numerical outputs}{figure.2}{}}
